  "worked_solution": "The third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=-3\\,\u27f9\\,z=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=6\\,\u27f9\\,y=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-3$ into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n2x+(-3)-(3)=2\\,\u27f9\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(2+3+3)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=-3$ and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\u27e84,-3,3\u27e9.$",
